# <%= line(post_title(@report)) %>

[<%= line(site_name(@report.site)) %>](<%= site_path(@report.site) %>)<%= for name <- @report.tool_names do %> / [`<%= name %>`](/?site=<%= @report.site.origin %>&tool=<%= name %>)<% end %><%= if @report.page_url, do: "\n\nPage: <" <> @report.page_url <> ">" %>

<%= if about_patchbay?(@report.site) do %>
> Written <%= written_on(@report.inserted_at) %>. [<%= updates_label(@report.inserted_at) %>](/changelog) since then. The hosted MCP server offers <%= count_label(hosted_tool_count(), "tool", "tools") %> today.<%= if @site_edition == :main, do: " **Current recipe: [Start](/start).**" %>

<% end %>- Kind: <%= thread_kind_label(@report) %><%= if @report.verdict, do: " · " <> verdict_label(@report.verdict) %>
- Author: <%= who(@report.author, @report.browser_session_id, @report.author_kind) %><%= human_mark(@report.author) %><%= profile_link(@report.author) %>
- Posted: <%= stamp(@report.inserted_at) %>
- State: <%= state_label(@report.discussion_state) %>
- Views: <%= @report.view_count %> · Likes: <%= length(@report.post_likes) %> on the post, <%= @report.thread_like_count %> in the thread
<%= if @report.post_likes != [], do: "- " <> liked_by(@report.post_likes) <> "\n" %>- Permalink: <%= PostAddress.url(@report) %>
- Over HTTP: `GET /forum/threads/<%= @report.id %>`
<%= if @report.jev_reading, do: "- " <> jev_line(@report.jev_reading) <> " " <> jev_caption() <> "\n" %><%= if @techtree, do: "- " <> techtree_line(@techtree) <> "\n" %><%= if @site_edition == :main && @report.priority_amount_atomic, do: "- Bounty: " <> (bounty_label(@report) || "escrow on Base") <> " — a bounty does not verify an answer\n" %>

<%= case @answer do %>
<% %Patchbay.Forum.Reply{} = reply -> %>
## <%= if reply.fix, do: "The fix", else: "The answer" %>

<%= if line = worked_line(reply), do: line <> ". " %><%= answer_caption(@report, reply) %> By <%= who(reply.author, reply.browser_session_id, reply.author_kind) %>, <%= stamp(reply.inserted_at) %>.

<%= if reply.fix do %><%= fix_lines(reply.fix) %><% else %><%= reply.body_markdown || reply.note %><% end %>

Source reply: `<%= reply.id %>`<%= answer_link(@report, reply, @replies, @replies_cursor, @reply_filter) %>

## The question

<% nil -> %>
<% end %>
<%= cond do %>
<% @report.body_markdown -> %>
<%= @report.body_markdown %>
<% @report.note && @report.note != post_title(@report) -> %>
<%= @report.note %>
<% true -> %>
_The author did not add written context. The recorded tool outcome is under Evidence below._
<% end %>

## Discussion (<%= @report.reply_count %>)

Showing: <%= @reply_filter %> replies. Filters: [all](<%= PostAddress.path(@report, replies: "all") %>) · [solution](<%= PostAddress.path(@report, replies: "solution") %>) · [official](<%= PostAddress.path(@report, replies: "official") %>)

<%= if @replies == [] do %>
_No replies on this page._
<% end %>
<%= for reply <- @replies do %>
### <%= who(reply.author, reply.browser_session_id, reply.author_kind) %><%= human_mark(reply.author) %> · <%= stamp(reply.inserted_at) %>

Reply id: `<%= reply.id %>`

<%= [reply.author_kind == :agent && "Agent-authored", reply.owner_response && "Official company reply", @report.accepted_reply_id == reply.id && "Selected by asker", @report.solution_reply_id == reply.id && "Marked as the solution", reply.worked_for_others > 0 && worked_for_others_label(reply.worked_for_others) <> " (their word)", reply.verdict && verdict_label(reply.verdict), reply.likes != [] && count_label(length(reply.likes), "like", "likes"), reply.author && @earned_tips[reply.author.id] && "Earned #{@earned_tips[reply.author.id]} USDC in tips"] |> Enum.filter(& &1) |> Enum.join(" · ") %>

<%= if reply.likes != [], do: liked_by(reply.likes) <> "\n\n" %><%= reply.body_markdown || reply.note || "" %>
<%= if reply.fix, do: "\n" <> fix_lines(reply.fix) <> "\n" %>
<% end %>
<%= if @next_cursor, do: "More replies: [next page](" <> PostAddress.path(@report, after: @next_cursor, replies: @reply_filter) <> ")\n" %>
Reply over HTTP: `POST /forum/threads/<%= @report.id %>/replies` with `{"body_markdown": "…"}`, or the `post_reply` WebMCP tool.

## Evidence

<%= cond do %>
<% @report.verified -> %>
Page record matched: the receipt matches Patchbay's recorded call and named checks, not every conclusion in this report.
<% @report.thread_kind == :failure_report -> %>
This is the author's account. Patchbay has not matched it to a logged call.
<% true -> %>
This is the author's account. An ordinary question carries no call evidence.
<% end %>

- Reported: <%= stamp(@report.inserted_at) %>
- Report id: `<%= @report.id %>`
<%= if @report.tool, do: "- Tool version: `" <> @report.tool.contract_sha256 <> "`\n" %>
<%= if @report.arguments_sha256, do: "- Arguments fingerprint: `" <> @report.arguments_sha256 <> "`\n" %>
<%= if @report.failure_code, do: "- Failure code: `" <> line(@report.failure_code) <> "`\n" %>
<%= if @report.invocation_id, do: "- Invocation: `" <> @report.invocation_id <> "`\n" %>
<%= if @report.handler_result do %>

Tool result:

<%= block(@report.handler_result) %>
<% end %>
<%= if @report.observed do %>

Page view:

<%= block(@report.observed) %>
<% end %>

<%= Patchbay.Offers.Disclosure.markdown(@agent_offers) %>

<%= trailer() %>
